The conflict error returned here leaves the directory copied above behind. In root compatibility mode, table lookup also reads name-derived `.lance` directories, so a failed concurrent rename still publishes a durable destination: one caller returns `Ok`, the other returns `ConcurrentModification`, but both new names are readable. A failed rename must not mutate visible namespace state. Copy into reader-hidden staging and publish or roll it back as part of the conflict-aware protocol; if that cannot be guaranteed for root-directory listing, keep rename unsupported there.

This is the current projection of [the earlier atomicity finding](https://github.com/lance-format/lance/pull/6975#discussion_r3781416801).

